     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. The usual maximum is 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day, and a single dose is typically 500\u20131,000 mg, up to 850 mg three times daily. A dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals**\n- Another dose, such as 1,700 mg total daily split into divided doses\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that. I'd also want a note on the order giving the clinical rationale. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
